// TEST: Quantity Declaration And Use
// `Unit speed: mps` declares a QUANTITY: a nominal identity entailing the
// dims of mps. Introduction positions stay permissive (a bare literal
// initializes a Float<speed> binding), and a quantity-carrying value flows
// freely into a STRUCTURAL (non-nominal) slot of the same dims.
Unit meters
Unit seconds
Unit mps = meters / seconds
Unit speed: mps
let v: Float<speed> = 4.0
let w: Float<mps> = v + 1.0
// EXPECT: v = 4
// EXPECT: w = 5
